	<!-- Campaign option hover tooltips (full descriptions the shortened labels drop) -->
	<string id="RBM_CON_050" text="Multiplier on the gold-and-spoils cost to upgrade a troop. 0 turns the spoils system off and makes upgrades free. Default 1.00." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_051" text="Multiplier on the worth of the kit your men salvage from a battlefield. Default 1.00." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_052" text="How many pieces of kit a single soldier can carry off a field. Default 3." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_053" text="Chance a man steps over a piece of kit one tier beneath him, leaving it for greener troops. Default 0.50." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_055" text="Days of food a man buys when he passes through a settlement. 0 stops him buying any. Default 20." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_056" text="Share of a day's wage a man spends to feed himself for a day. Default 0.50." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_057" text="A day's wage a man drinks away for each day he sits idle in a settlement. Default 1.50." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_058" text="How much Prosperity, or a village's Hearth, a gold moves at a settlement, both ways: trade and carousing there add it, its militia's wages and every good it produces drain it. Default 0.02." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_059" text="Share of a raid's plunder its soldiers keep for themselves as spoils. Default 0.25." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_061" text="Days of keep a stack holds in its purse before upkeep spends the surplus: this many days of its wage and its field maintenance together. Default 20." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_063" text="Days a stack waits after buying a luxury before it splurges again. Default 20." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_064" text="Chance each idle hour that an over-cap stack buys a luxury from the settlement. Default 0.02." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_066" text="Share of a beaten enemy's killed and wounded spoils the victors carry off; the rest is lost. Default 0.75." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_067" text="Wage Base per Tier" />
	<string id="RBM_CON_068" text="Daily wage is this base value multiplied by the troop's tier, replacing the vanilla wage. Zero keeps vanilla wages. Default 20." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_062" text="Reset to Default" />
	<string id="RBM_CON_070" text="Upgrade Near Town" />
	<string id="RBM_CON_071" text="Upgrade Supply Range" />
	<string id="RBM_CON_072" text="How near, in map units, a friendly or neutral town must be for a party to upgrade its troops. Needs 'Upgrade Near Town' on. Default 30." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_073" text="Heal Cost per Tier" />
	<string id="RBM_CON_074" text="Gold a wounded man's stack pays to mend him faster while resting in a settlement, scaled by his tier. Zero stops paid healing. Default 10." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_075" text="Heal Rate per Hour" />
	<string id="RBM_CON_076" text="Most of a stack's wounded that paid healing mends in one hour, so a deep purse buys a faster recovery, not an instant one. Default 0.05." />
	<string id="RBM_CON_077" text="Militia Wage Modifier" />
	<string id="RBM_CON_078" text="Share of their gear-based wage a settlement's militia cost the place that keeps them, drawn from Prosperity or Hearth. Zero makes militia free to garrison. Default 0.20." />
		<string id="RBM_CON_079" text="Leader's Cut" />
		<string id="RBM_CON_080" text="Base share of the spoils a party's men gather -- off a battlefield, a raid or a sack -- that their leader skims into his own purse as gold before the rest settles into the stacks. Multiplied by the leader's clan tier plus one, so a tier-0 or clanless leader takes this share once and a tier-6 house seven times it. Zero leaves the men all they take. Default 0.05." />
		<string id="RBM_CON_081" text="Daily Maintenance" />
		<string id="RBM_CON_082" text="Daily upkeep per soldier as a share of his whole kit's worth -- gear, horse and harness. Paid first from the men's own spoils; any shortfall falls to the party leader's gold. Zero stops maintenance. Default 0.005." />
		<string id="RBM_CON_083" text="Recruit Maintenance Days" />
		<string id="RBM_CON_084" text="Days of maintenance a recruit mustered from a village or town brings in his stack's purse, priced off the same daily upkeep. 0 seeds nothing. Default 5." />
		<string id="RBM_CON_085" text="Maintenance to Prosperity" />
		<string id="RBM_CON_086" text="Share of a party's daily troop maintenance that settles into the Prosperity of the nearest city or castle, never a village. Scaled by Prosperity per Gold. Default 0.50." />
		<string id="RBM_CON_087" text="Buy Mounts For Upgrades" />
		<string id="RBM_CON_088" text="Upgrading into a mounted troop no longer needs a horse in the baggage train and consumes none; the horse and harness are paid for in gold/spoils instead. Off restores the vanilla horse-item requirement. Default on." />
		<string id="RBM_CON_089" text="Mercenary Maintenance Share" />
		<string id="RBM_CON_090" text="Share of daily maintenance a mercenary company under a kingdom's pay meets from its own spoils; its employer covers the rest, any shortfall falling to the party leader's gold. Default 0.50." />
		<string id="RBM_CON_091" text="Independent Maintenance Share" />
		<string id="RBM_CON_092" text="Share of daily maintenance an independent clan -- one sworn to no kingdom -- meets from its own spoils; any shortfall falls to the party leader's gold. Sworn vassals and rulers pay none from their purses. Default 1.00." />
